1
00:00:10,257 --> 00:00:12,616
I'm sorry for the trouble
earlier, Comrade Roong.

2
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,119
Especially now that Comrade Fah has forbidden
anyone from entering or leaving the base.

3
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,879
But that household is in serious condition.

4
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:18,799
That's why we had to ask you to come help.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,359
It's alright. The villagers'
lives are what matter most.

6
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,656
If there's any problem,
I'll speak with Comrade Fah myself.

7
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,839
Um... Comrade Roong.

8
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:25,840
We'd better go this way.

9
00:00:25,841 --> 00:00:27,976
There are too many people that way.
Someone might see us.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,240
If we go this way,
we won't run into Comrade Fah either.

11
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,120
Ever since Comrade Ploeng died,

12
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,200
the base has felt so quiet and lonely.

13
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,920
How has Comrade Bai Tong been lately?

14
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,600
She barely ate the food I gave her.

15
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:52,480
Comrade Gaun Hin.

16
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,959
Where are you going?

17
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,919
Oh, I'm taking documents for the courier-

18
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,400
-to deliver for printing in the city.

19
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,280
Go and come back quickly.

20
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,480
Be careful.

21
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,840
Comrades

22
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,919
we caught the person who killed Ploeng.

23
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:06,999
Comrades.

24
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,400
Comrades, we caught the
person who killed Ploeng.

25
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
"When Light Fades"
(Episode 6)

26
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:04,520
Dan.

27
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,280
Answer whatever I ask.

28
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,440
Because if you talk,

29
00:02:12,719 --> 00:02:13,918
you won't have to get hurt.

30
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,120
Mm.

31
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,200
Comrade Fah! Comrade Fah!

32
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,720
Comrade Fah.

33
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,280
Comrade Fah.

34
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,799
Comrade Roong is gone.

35
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,960
Since when?

36
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,440
Yang Sue said
a villager was in critical condition

37
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,280
and urgently needed medicine.

38
00:02:26,281 --> 00:02:27,521
So Roong rushed out right away.

39
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,320
I told her to stay inside the base.

40
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,159
And where is Yang Sue now?

41
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:35,319
The villagers said he left
with the cabbage truck

42
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:36,560
before sunrise.

43
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,960
And now Comrade Roong is missing.

44
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:41,720
Don't tell anyone yet.

45
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,680
I don't want the people
in the village to panic.

46
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:55,960
Whoa...

47
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,600
that was close.

48
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,439
Just now, Comrade Yue seemed to turn
and look this way too.

49
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,000
I'm not sure if he saw us or not.

50
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,480
Sorry, I lost myself for a second.

51
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:08,720
This guy...

52
00:03:08,721 --> 00:03:10,519
he's probably the one
who killed Comrade Ploeng.

53
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,039
You know him too?

54
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:12,960
Yes.

55
00:03:12,961 --> 00:03:14,401
He was my neighbor when I was a kid.

56
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,279
Doesn't matter how you know him.

57
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,959
You'd better stay away from him.

58
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,520
You might get dragged into it too.

59
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,600
Hey, Comrade Saeng.

60
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:27,320
Don't even think about
going to see Dan, Comrade Saeng.

61
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,000
Go on, get going.

62
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,520
What brings you here, Comrade?

63
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,240
Or do you need some medicine?

64
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,800
I came to get supplies
to treat the prisoner's gunshot wound.

65
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,240
Get them ready for me.

66
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,760
Yes.

67
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,199
And...

68
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,759
Are you going to
remove the bullet yourself?

69
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,320
Would you like me to do it for you?

70
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,160
It's alright.

71
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,480
I'll take it out myself.

72
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,640
Comrade Yue.

73
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,280
Comrade Ying.

74
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,959
I came to speak with you about-

75
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,400
-my mother's condition for a moment.

76
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,480
How is she?

77
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:41,920
Has she gotten any better?

78
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,160
We got medicine from the base,

79
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,240
so we've managed to keep her stable.

80
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,520
It's done.

81
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:02,320
Has he admitted yet that he was
the one who killed Comrade Ploeng?

82
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,360
Not yet.

83
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,760
A son of a high-ranking
military officer like you.

84
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:15,600
Why would you choose to be stationed here?

85
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,680
What do you want?

86
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,240
Getting yourself captured like this...

87
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,040
Was it your plan?

88
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:59,780
Comrade Roong's disappearance...

89
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,000
That was because of you too, wasn't it?

90
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:46,080
Whatever you're hoping for,

91
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,280
you won't get your way.

92
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:55,120
You still don't know

93
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,200
who's going to be disappointed.

94
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,240
Vin.
Dan.

95
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,120
How did you end up here?

96
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,640
I came here on purpose.

97
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,720
I wanted to see you, Vin.

98
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,880
Aunt La-Or feels the same.

99
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,760
She misses you so much that
she's fallen sick many times.

100
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,680
She told me

101
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,200
to bring you home no matter what.

102
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,039
But it's not that easy, Dan.

103
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,040
It's not that hard, Vin.

104
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,720
Just say the word,

105
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,200
and I'll take you out myself.

106
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,160
Worry about saving yourself first.

107
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:29,760
Get up.

108
00:09:29,761 --> 00:09:31,239
Hey! Let go of Vin!

109
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,240
Stay out of this.

110
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:33,640
Don't touch my people.

111
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,480
Vin.

112
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,119
Can I have five minutes? Just five minutes.

113
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,120
Five minutes?

114
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,239
That could get you killed.

115
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,360
What if someone else sees?

116
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,080
Have you thought about that?

117
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,760
Hey!

118
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,440
What were you doing in there?

119
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,440
Treating the prisoner's wound.

120
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:01,800
I forgot something inside.

121
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,280
Where is it then?

122
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,520
It wasn't there.

123
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,399
I dropped it somewhere else.

124
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,040
Then why did you come together?

125
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:23,800
And what rule says two people can't come together?

126
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:54,120
What are you to that soldier?

127
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
He was a neighbor.

128
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,240
We knew each other when we were kids.

129
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:01,240
But he moved away
when I was still in primary school.

130
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,960
We never spoke again after that.

131
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:15,440
He's like an older brother.

132
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:23,880
But this one isn't.

133
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,480
Promise me

134
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:32,000
you won't go see that soldier again.

135
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:37,320
If anyone finds out,
it'll be very dangerous.

136
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,640
Let me help you then.

137
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,800
Get this over with.

138
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:25,440
May I hold your hand?

139
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:38,760
Who is Aunt La-Or?

140
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,720
My mother.

141
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:47,200
There's still a lot about
you that I don't know.

142
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,520
Not knowing isn't a problem.

143
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,400
We still have our whole lives together.

144
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:57,200
I will tell you little by little,
and you can teach me too.

145
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,920
Everything I know, I've already taught you.

146
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,680
Except this... You still
have a lot to teach me.

147
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,680
Pack up quickly.

148
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,599
I just found out-

149
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:42,359
-that grinding stones and
mixing them with honey

150
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,160
can make a color like this.

151
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,160
If I put this on for Father to see,

152
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:50,880
he'd definitely say I look cute.

153
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,680
Comrade Ploeng hasn't gone far at all.

154
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:04,760
He only changed where he lives—

155
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:08,000
now he lives in Comrade Bai Tong's heart.

156
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:12,399
And you still have us,
you have Comrade Saeng,

157
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:14,800
and all the comrades beside you too.

158
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:26,760
What are you doing here?

159
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:30,400
Where is it?

160
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,040
Comrade Fah,

161
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,359
stop right now!

162
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,439
Don't take my father's things!

163
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:40,920
Hey!
Don't take them!

164
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,720
Bai Tong!

165
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,719
- Don't!
- Hey!

166
00:14:45,743 --> 00:14:46,903
This is not Comrade Ploeng's.

167
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,800
This belongs to the Party.

168
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:52,920
And what is this, huh?

169
00:14:58,760 --> 00:14:59,840
That's enough, Comrade Fah.

170
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:02,080
Wearing makeup and doing hair like this...

171
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,600
It looks like discipline is gone now.

172
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:08,119
If I see it again, I won't let it slide.

173
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,159
In what capacity are you saying that?

174
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,920
You're not the leader of the base.

175
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:14,880
Comrade Ploeng would
never threaten anyone like this.

176
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:32,800
Sila.

177
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,280
Mada.

178
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,200
Ravin.

179
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,160
Chai Chan.

180
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,640
Police Lieutenant...

181
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:57,560
Rapee Chai Chan.

182
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,599
I knew it.

183
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,120
Comrade Fah.

184
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,440
I just got word from Comrade Roong.

185
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:09,080
What is it?

186
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:11,120
Comrade Roong was captured by the soldiers.

187
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,359
They sent word saying--

188
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,800
that they want to exchange hostages.

189
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Go get Comrade Yue
to the meeting right now.

190
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,680
What in the actual fuck?

191
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:39,240
You and Comrade Yue take control of them.

192
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,399
Have armed men ready.

193
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,480
Lock down the area.

194
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,200
If they try anything dishonest,

195
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,439
we'll be ready to strike back.

196
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,120
Everything must be finished tonight.

197
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,280
Why?

198
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,640
You have a problem?

199
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,200
I'll take care of it.

200
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:20,440
Wait.

201
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:26,840
You and Comrade Saeng

202
00:17:26,841 --> 00:17:28,481
seem a little too close, don't you think?

203
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,680
Tell me then—what should I do?

204
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:52,199
Ravin ChaiChan.

205
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,320
Police Lieutenant Rapee ChaiChan
Mrs. La-Or Chai Chan.

206
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:59,080
I'm going to take this all the way.

207
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:00,879
Hey, where are you?

208
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:01,600
Hey!

209
00:18:01,601 --> 00:18:03,479
Where's your boss?

210
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,639
- Bring your boss out here to talk to me!
- Stop, stop! Hey!

211
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,159
This bastard right here!

212
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,160
Stop!

213
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,079
You know what?

214
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:12,519
Because of you, our fathers
died in prison for nothing.

215
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,600
They never even got a
chance to prove a damn thing.

216
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:21,119
Hey! Hey! Hey!

217
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,839
Hey, come out here and talk to me!

218
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,160
Watch your mouth, kid.

219
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,279
The lower court ruled that
your fathers were guilty.

220
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,479
Why blame the police?

221
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:29,480
How can you say that?

222
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,599
And if the court overturns it and says-

223
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:32,639
-my father was innocent,

224
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:33,280
how are you going to take responsibility?

225
00:18:33,281 --> 00:18:36,599
The evidence was clear at the time,
so I had to do my duty.

226
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:37,799
You bastard!

227
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:40,039
What the hell did you
just say, you bastard?!

228
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:41,120
Argh!

229
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:45,840
Let me go! Let go! Let go!

230
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,840
Get him out of here.

231
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,560
Hey, stop!

232
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:58,040
This isn't over, bastard! This is not over!

233
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,719
I'll get you back.

234
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:01,960
Go!

235
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,280
I'll handle it myself.

236
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,200
How are you going to handle it? Tell me.

237
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,959
Why the hell isn't he here yet?

238
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:14,960
This is taking forever.

239
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:20,279
If we kill him, how are
we any different from him?

240
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:21,799
I don't care whether
we're different or not.

241
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,279
I only care that he pays for it.

242
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,839
I'll get rid of them all.

243
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:26,360
Why are you chickening out now?

244
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,600
He's here!

245
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:33,880
Ready?

246
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,439
Wait... I'm not doing this
anymore. Let's go back.

247
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,559
If you won't do it, I will.

248
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,560
You...

249
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:02,200
Argh!

250
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:10,080
Go to hell!

251
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,040
Sin!

252
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:23,920
You!

253
00:20:23,921 --> 00:20:25,000
Don't hurt my friend!

254
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,800
Don't hurt my friend!

255
00:20:57,400 --> 00:21:01,480
Aagh! Aagh! Aagh!

256
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,679
Sin! Sin! Sin! Look at me!

257
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,279
Look at me, Sin!

258
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,560
Sin, look at me!

259
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:30,680
Run!

260
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:31,840
Run!

261
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:33,800
Run! Go!

262
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:35,280
Go!

263
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,200
Go!

264
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:50,880
Sin!

265
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:53,760
Or do you want him to find out

266
00:21:53,761 --> 00:21:55,081
that you and I killed his father,

267
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:57,280
and wait for him to come after us?

268
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:04,120
I'm telling you,

269
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:08,440
we should nip it in the bud.

270
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,040
Nop.

271
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,480
Whether you want to
be the leader of the base

272
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:27,119
or whatever else you want to do,

273
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:28,120
I don't care.

274
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,160
But this matter...

275
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,040
Let me handle it myself.

276
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:21,320
Hey!

277
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,880
What's wrong with you?

278
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,040
Why did you hurt yourself?

279
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:52,080
Are you so jealous that
you ended up crying?

280
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,240
Why are you acting like a child?

281
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:59,200
I had a small argument with Comrade Fah.

282
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:01,600
It's nothing.

283
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:09,360
Come on, I'll treat your wound.

284
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:16,600
Go back first.

285
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,960
I'll follow after you.

286
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:15,160
When you get out,

287
00:25:16,360 --> 00:25:17,760
don't ever come back here again.

288
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:24,240
Whether I come back or not, I don't know.

289
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:28,000
But I'm definitely taking
my person with me.

290
00:25:35,920 --> 00:25:37,240
Does Vin know

291
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:39,400
that he belongs to you?

292
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,360
Anything that's in the wrong place

293
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:46,600
doesn't stay there for long.

294
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:50,160
If fooling yourself makes
you happy, then go ahead.

295
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:08,400
Why are you sleeping here?

296
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:13,440
I was worried.

297
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:16,240
Did you have a serious
fight with Comrade Fah?

298
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:21,360
Go get some sleep.

299
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,840
I took this from the medical hut.

300
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:31,880
I need to hurry and return it.

301
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:41,280
Come here.

302
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:43,480
Even now, you're still shy?

303
00:28:54,320 --> 00:28:56,160
Did you ever feel so happy--

304
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:00,640
that you're afraid it'll end badly?

305
00:29:08,560 --> 00:29:11,400
People either part while
alive... or part by death.

306
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,280
And we never know when we'll part.

307
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:16,559
If we spend all our time being afraid

308
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:17,920
until we can't do anything at all,

309
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:19,880
wouldn't it be more regretful

310
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,720
if we never tried with all our heart?

311
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:36,840
Then what should I do?

312
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:42,000
You have to keep collecting
happiness little by little.

313
00:29:42,520 --> 00:29:43,440
Like this—

314
00:29:43,441 --> 00:29:45,000
I'm doing it right now.

315
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:36,720
That's enough.

316
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:42,960
And you don't need to be jealous of
that soldier anymore.

317
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:46,000
I love only this person.

318
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:50,360
The murderer is coming.

319
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:28,200
I'm sorry.

320
00:33:19,400 --> 00:33:20,520
Go tell Vin

321
00:33:21,200 --> 00:33:23,160
that the person who
loves him is waiting outside.

322
00:33:30,840 --> 00:33:31,920
You're alright, aren't you?

323
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:30,439
What did that soldier say just now?

324
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:31,600
Did you get what he said?

325
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:42,360
Oh, Comrade Saeng, how did you get here?

326
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:48,400
So?

327
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:50,040
When did it start?

328
00:34:57,640 --> 00:34:59,120
Can you please not tell anyone?

329
00:35:00,480 --> 00:35:01,280
I don't want Comrade Saeng

330
00:35:01,281 --> 00:35:02,680
to get into trouble because of me.

331
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:08,639
The good thing about
being a courier, Comrade,

332
00:35:08,640 --> 00:35:10,239
is first of all,

333
00:35:10,240 --> 00:35:11,879
I run everywhere in the forest,

334
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,400
outside the forest, and in the city.

335
00:35:14,720 --> 00:35:17,039
I meet all kinds of people everywhere.

336
00:35:17,040 --> 00:35:20,199
Whether it's couples with an age gap
and things like that,

337
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:22,080
or men who like men,
women who like women...

338
00:35:22,880 --> 00:35:25,160
I honestly don't think there's
anything strange about it.

339
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:28,240
And...

340
00:35:29,720 --> 00:35:30,880
do you despise it, Comrade?

341
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:36,560
I think it's simply about
two people loving each other.

342
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,080
There's nothing ugly about it.

343
00:35:41,040 --> 00:35:42,120
So what now?

344
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:44,560
Anything to say?

345
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:47,160
Do you love each other that much, huh?

346
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:52,999
Wow... seeing Comrade Yue blush like this,

347
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:54,519
I can die with my eyes closed now.

348
00:35:54,520 --> 00:35:55,520
I'm off.

349
00:35:56,760 --> 00:35:57,960
Hurry and catch up.

350
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:01,120
Comrade Phu Pha.

351
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:26,760
Dan.

352
00:36:26,840 --> 00:36:27,840
Father.

353
00:36:30,680 --> 00:36:31,680
How did you get here?

354
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:34,519
Whatever you're
planning to do, just tell me.

355
00:36:34,520 --> 00:36:35,560
Is that so hard?

356
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:39,920
If...

357
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:43,400
If I had told you I was going in there
to become a hostage,

358
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:45,200
would you have let me go?

359
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:47,360
And what were you doing in there?

360
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:50,120
Helping the students.

361
00:36:51,320 --> 00:36:53,760
There are students in the
jungle all over the country.

362
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:56,440
But you deliberately
chose to go to that base.

363
00:36:57,737 --> 00:36:59,096
Does this have anything
to do with the information.

364
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:00,599
I asked you to investigate before?

365
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:02,000
Um... no, it's not related, Father.

366
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:05,879
As for Baan Saeng Dao Base,

367
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:07,760
it's the base closest to
the main headquarters.

368
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:10,440
If this place falls, the
rest will collapse too.

369
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:12,520
I just wanted to-

370
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:14,479
-settle things properly, that's all.

371
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:15,920
Don't think about attacking anymore.

372
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:18,400
Right now, the higher-ups have a policy

373
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:20,080
to bring the students back in.

374
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:21,760
Bring the students back?

375
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:23,120
Yes.
I mean...

376
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:27,080
Does that mean we're
not going to fight anymore?

377
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:28,800
Yes.

378
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,480
The leaders have realized-

379
00:37:31,280 --> 00:37:33,360
-that chasing each other like this

380
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:36,720
is the same as killing our own children
and grandchildren.

381
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,440
Bringing them back out of the forest

382
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:41,880
will make them useful to the nation.

383
00:37:51,160 --> 00:37:53,399
Why are you making dots
like that, Comrade Saeng?

384
00:37:53,400 --> 00:37:55,280
I'm not a spotted deer.

385
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:04,240
A spotted deer or a cat?

386
00:38:06,520 --> 00:38:08,600
Then do it properly, Comrade Saeng.

387
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:11,239
Stay still. I'll fix it.

388
00:38:11,240 --> 00:38:16,599
Comrade Bai Tong's
flower crown is finished.

389
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:18,840
How is it? Look in the mirror.

390
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:22,760
So pretty.

391
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:27,160
Of course. Cause I made it.

392
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:34,440
What are you doing?

393
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:37,600
The order appointing the
new base leader has arrived.

394
00:38:50,520 --> 00:38:52,359
I feel greatly honored

395
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:54,400
to be trusted with
taking care of this base.

396
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:58,000
And I promise that
everything will remain the same.

397
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:00,959
But some loose matters may be adjusted-

398
00:39:00,960 --> 00:39:03,000
-to better follow the rules.

399
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:14,319
And the rules begin now!

400
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:17,439
When the leader is speaking,
everyone should listen,

401
00:39:17,440 --> 00:39:19,240
not turn and look elsewhere.

402
00:39:20,320 --> 00:39:22,160
And I'd like two or three comrades

403
00:39:22,280 --> 00:39:23,519
to help me move Comrade Ploeng's

404
00:39:23,520 --> 00:39:24,560
belongings from the house.

405
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:28,800
Because I'll likely-

406
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:30,640
-be moving in there

407
00:39:31,600 --> 00:39:33,079
as required by the position.

408
00:39:33,080 --> 00:39:34,720
I'll speak on behalf of Comrade Bai Tong.

409
00:39:34,960 --> 00:39:36,199
Comrade Bai Tong has
lived there since birth.

410
00:39:36,200 --> 00:39:37,200
And?

411
00:39:37,337 --> 00:39:38,297
If she gets moved out now,

412
00:39:38,321 --> 00:39:40,081
Comrade Bai Tong
won't be able to handle it.

413
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:41,560
That's right.

414
00:39:41,680 --> 00:39:43,000
Let Comrade Bai Tong rest first.

415
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:44,959
Let her recover emotionally first.

416
00:39:44,960 --> 00:39:45,720
No.
It must be now.

417
00:39:46,681 --> 00:39:48,039
- Why?
- Damn it.

418
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:49,119
You really meddle too much.

419
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:50,239
You two, follow me.

420
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:51,240
Now.

421
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:52,640
Hey!

422
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:07,599
You two, move everything out.

423
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,120
Don't leave a single piece behind. Go!

424
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,520
Don't take my father's things!

425
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:13,560
- Hey!
- No!

426
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:16,520
- No! Where are you taking my father's things?!
- Bai Tong.

427
00:40:22,240 --> 00:40:23,759
Don't take my father's things!

428
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:24,760
Hey!

429
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:31,719
Don't take anything away!

430
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:32,480
Let go!

431
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:34,480
Bai Tong!

432
00:40:34,920 --> 00:40:36,319
You won't even spare a child, huh?

433
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:38,360
You really love meddling
in my business, don't you?

434
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:48,880
This is already more than enough.

435
00:40:49,640 --> 00:40:50,879
Don't make this a bigger deal.

436
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:52,320
Why are you staring at me like that?

437
00:40:52,440 --> 00:40:54,080
Got a problem? Huh?

438
00:40:59,800 --> 00:41:00,800
Bai Tong!

439
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:03,680
Aah! You little brat!

440
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:10,599
Wearing makeup and fixing your hair like-

441
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:12,280
-this is against Party rules, understand?

442
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:19,280
Son of a bitch!
Bai Tong!

443
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,120
Ouch!

444
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:30,160
- Bai Tong!
- Sin.

445
00:41:30,440 --> 00:41:31,560
If you don't stop right now,

446
00:41:32,440 --> 00:41:33,479
you'll see.

447
00:41:33,480 --> 00:41:34,560
You...

448
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:57,039
Am I pretty, Father?

449
00:41:57,040 --> 00:41:58,840
Wow...

450
00:41:59,520 --> 00:42:01,360
very pretty, my dear.

451
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:04,239
But you know

452
00:42:04,240 --> 00:42:07,600
you can't wear flowers like
that and go walking outside.

453
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:10,679
But why, Father?

454
00:42:10,680 --> 00:42:12,520
I can let only Comrade Ying see it.

455
00:42:14,640 --> 00:42:18,160
If every woman comrade here
wanted to be pretty like you,

456
00:42:18,920 --> 00:42:21,800
and wanted to wear flowers like you,
every one of them,

457
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:24,320
what do you think would happen?

458
00:42:27,640 --> 00:42:29,239
If all the women comrades

459
00:42:29,240 --> 00:42:30,999
picked flowers to wear every day,

460
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:32,880
then there wouldn't be
any flowers left, right?

461
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:35,320
That's true.

462
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:37,399
Flowers...

463
00:42:37,400 --> 00:42:40,159
they're useful because they're beautiful.

464
00:42:40,160 --> 00:42:42,160
And they have other uses too.

465
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:44,240
But here,

466
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:47,360
I see them as something unnecessary.

467
00:42:49,080 --> 00:42:50,480
Bai Tong, my child.

468
00:42:51,520 --> 00:42:53,359
I want you to be a good example

469
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:54,800
to the women comrades here.

470
00:42:55,880 --> 00:42:57,240
Live simply,

471
00:42:57,720 --> 00:42:59,280
and not extravagantly.

472
00:43:00,440 --> 00:43:01,920
You understand me, don't you?

473
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:10,639
Then I'll pick flowers from the ground-

474
00:43:10,640 --> 00:43:12,040
-and wear them only for Father.

475
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:14,880
That's my girl.

476
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:16,720
Very good.

477
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:19,800
Very good for
understanding things so easily.

478
00:43:43,880 --> 00:43:44,920
You hit me that hard...

479
00:43:45,440 --> 00:43:47,040
you really hate me that much, don't you?

480
00:43:47,280 --> 00:43:49,040
I only asked what you
two are to each other.
